          "stage": "final",
          "status": "succeeded",
          "verdict": "block",
          "summary": "The study lacks fundamental methodological rigor: no proportional hazards assumption testing, no confounder selection rationale or adjustment for measured confounders beyond age/severity, missing variable definitions, no descriptive statistics, and insufficient model diagnostics. These issues render results uninterpretable and require substantial revision before the manuscript can be considered for promotion.",
          "findings": [
            {
              "id": "F1",
              "severity": "blocker",
              "category": "model_diagnostics",
              "title": "Missing proportional hazards assumption testing",
              "evidenceRefs": [
                "stats-run/diagnostics.json",
                "stats-run/stats-run.json"
              ],
              "whyItMatters": "Cox regression requires the proportional hazards assumption to produce valid hazard ratios. Without formal testing (e.g., Schoenfeld residuals, log-log plots), the reported treatment effect may be invalid or misleading.",
              "actionableFix": "Compute Schoenfeld residuals and report a global test for each covariate and overall. Provide scaled Schoenfeld residual plots or a log-log survival plot to assess proportionality.",
              "reentryPoint": "execution",
              "deterministicVerification": "Check diagnostics.json for presence of 'proportional_hazards_tests' or similar field with p-values.",
              "confidence": 0.95
            },
            {
              "id": "F2",
              "severity": "blocker",
              "category": "variables",
              "title": "Variable definitions and coding are missing",
              "evidenceRefs": [
                "manuscript.md"
              ],
              "whyItMatters": "Interpretation of hazard ratios depends entirely on variable coding: whether treatment is binary, how aging is scaled (per year, per decade), whether severity is continuous or categorical, and what event/survival_time represent. Without definitions, the numeric results are meaningless.",
              "actionableFix": "Provide explicit definitions for every variable: measurement unit, category labels, reference group if applicable, and data source. For continuous variables, state the unit of increment corresponding to the HR.",
              "reentryPoint": "manuscript",
              "deterministicVerification": null,
              "confidence": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "F3",
              "severity": "blocker",
              "category": "study_design",
              "title": "Insufficient adjustment for confounding",
              "evidenceRefs": [
                "manuscript.md",
                "stats-run/stats-run.json"
              ],
              "whyItMatters": "Observational studies require a plausible confounder selection strategy (e.g., DAG, literature-based) to reduce bias. Using only age and severity likely leaves substantial residual confounding, making the association between treatment and outcome unreliable.",
              "actionableFix": "Develop a causal diagram, identify a minimally sufficient adjustment set, and either include those variables in a multivariable model or use propensity score methods. Provide a sensitivity analysis for unmeasured confounding.",
              "reentryPoint": "protocol",
              "deterministicVerification": null,
              "confidence": 0.9
            },
            {
              "id": "F4",
              "severity": "major",
              "category": "missingness",
              "title": "Missing data handling not described",
              "evidenceRefs": [
                "manuscript.md"
              ],
              "whyItMatters": "Complete-case analysis (n=240) can introduce selection bias if missingness is related to exposure, outcome, or covariates. Without reporting the amount and pattern of missingness, readers cannot assess potential bias.",
              "actionableFix": "Report missingness proportions per variable, compare characteristics of excluded vs. included subjects, and consider multiple imputation or a sensitivity analysis (e.g., pattern-mixture model).",
              "reentryPoint": "analysis_spec",
              "deterministicVerification": null,
              "confidence": 0.85
            },
            {
              "id": "F5",
              "severity": "major",
              "category": "reporting",
              "title": "Lack of descriptive statistics",
              "evidenceRefs": [
                "manuscript.md"
              ],
              "whyItMatters": "Without a baseline characteristics table (Table 1), it is impossible to assess comparability of treatment groups, potential confounding, or generalizability of the sample.",
              "actionableFix": "Include a table summarizing demographic and clinical features by treatment arm, with appropriate statistical comparisons (standardized differences preferred over p-values).",
              "reentryPoint": "manuscript",
              "deterministicVerification": null,
              "confidence": 0.95
            },
            {
              "id": "F6",
              "severity": "major",
              "category": "model_diagnostics",
              "title": "Insufficient model diagnostics beyond event count",
              "evidenceRefs": [
                "stats-run/diagnostics.json"
              ],
              "whyItMatters": "The only diagnostic provided is number of events (140) and predictors (3). Model fit, influential observations, or assumption checks (linearity, additivity) are absent, undermining trust in the estimates.",
              "actionableFix": "Report model fit statistics (e.g., concordance, R²), check for non-linearity (martingale residuals), and assess influential points (dfbetas).",
              "reentryPoint": "execution",
              "deterministicVerification": null,
              "confidence": 0.8
            },
            {
              "id": "F7",
              "severity": "minor",
              "category": "reproducibility",
              "title": "Data and analysis code not provided",
              "evidenceRefs": [
                "manuscript.md"
